Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; Register the glc: URL scheme for EVERY user of this PC (issue #199), so a
; gram page's "WAV N" link opens the .glc in the legacy replay tool.
; Machine-wide (HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE): import it ONCE, logged in as the
; administrator. Ordinary users then get the handler without importing
; anything, even where registry editing is blocked for them.
;
; STAND-ALONE PCs ONLY. Domain PCs get the handler from Group Policy (script
; under C:\Program Files\AAAC\, no -ExecutionPolicy switch); see
; theme/glc-launch/README.md. -ExecutionPolicy Bypass is here only because a
; stand-alone PC has no policy permitting the script.
;
; BEFORE IMPORTING: the path below must be where glc-launch.ps1 lives, and it
; must resolve for every user - a drive letter only works if that drive is
; mapped in each user's logon. A \\server\share path avoids that. Edit it if
; needed - every backslash written twice. See theme/glc-launch/README.md.

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Classes\glc]
@="URL:Gram replay link"
"URL Protocol"=""

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Classes\glc\shell]

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Classes\glc\shell\open]

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Classes\glc\shell\open\command]
@="powershell.exe -NoProfile -NonInteractive -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -WindowStyle Hidden -File \"N:\\legacy_config\\glc-launch.ps1\" \"%1\""
